 "summary": "This cluster is centered around various fungal strains, including F. yunnanensis, Z68, and Papiliotrema flavescens, which are all part of the Basidiomycota phylum. F. yunnanensis is associated with the FTR1 Iron Permease gene and has been affected by Magnesium sulfate. The strain Z68 has higher levels of potassium and zinc. Papiliotrema flavescens is linked to PDA, which has growth characteristics associated with this strain. The cluster also includes various chemicals, such as iron, tea infusion, and RPT, which are analyzed using methods like UHPLC-Q-Exactive/MS and DeepTMHMM.",
